00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.049 align:start position:0%
earlier this week the council held its  monthly meeting for November it started  with a presentation from Sam hull who  was representing the ownership of  Pegasus Golf Club he updated the council  about Pegasus hosting the NZ PGA  Championship Tournament for the next  three years and talked about future  plans to construct accommodation and  conference facilities at the golf course  [Music]  the council also formally adopted the  caillou town center plan 2028 and beyond  it promotes a vision of a vibrant town  center that embraces the river attracts  visitors and new businesses and creates  enjoyable public spaces for the first  time it also includes master plans for  the mix juice business areas that were  set aside following the Canterbury  earthquakes because of the large amount  of land available for development that's  considered a long-term plan and could  take the next 20 to 30 years to be fully  realized the council also approved a  submission on behalf of the Waimakariri  district to the draft regional public  transport plan this document plans for  the region's public transport needs for  the next 10 years and beyond our council  strongly advocated for higher frequency  services between christchurch and our  main towns we also ask that the  committee be more ambitious and trialing  new transport technologies and  developing demand responsive services  for our smaller or more remote  population centers the final monthly  council meeting for the year will be  held on Tuesday the 4th of December  [Music]
 

